{
 "_comment": "Land-use class table (#253): tag mapping and per-class defaults together. No class ships a fence default (every boundary is null). Furniture (#260): park ships bench_per_100m (benches on its paths); every other class ships null. highways is the default lamp spacing in blocks along the way, staggered either side, per OSM highway class; a class absent here (service, path, cycleway, steps, links) is not lit by inference, and a district profile or street convention beats it. Surface (#316): surface.unmapped_paving is the kind aerial paving takes off a mapped way (dirt, grass, or null to keep the aerial paving); surface.path_widen (#325) is the reach in blocks (1..6, or null) beside a mapped path within which aerial paving takes that path's own surface, so a path the map draws thin reads as wide as the aerial shows it (park 3; every other class null). Trees (#317, #368): trees.sources lists permitted evidence on park, rural and natural land (mapped points/rows, wood/scrub/forest within 2 blocks, lidar standing height >= 2m within 2 blocks, or lines: a hedge or lane corridor and the unmapped belt grown from it where first-return standing height is at least 2m). Aerial darkness is not lines evidence. Absent or null keeps existing sources. Aerial cover (#361): trees.cover is \"shade\" on park and rural so the cover test uses a lower brightness ceiling and a lower saturation floor (sunlit meadow scores low, dull shaded canopy scores high); absent or null keeps the ordinary cover test. It is not a trees.sources value. Species (#350): trees.species_weights is keyed by land-use class; natural uses placeholder oak 60 / birch 25 / dark_oak 15 for #318 tuning (not evidence); park and rural stay oak-only. Ground texture (#319): ground_texture pasture/meadow palettes on park, rural and natural enable rough grass and mottled dirt from aerial texture on meadow/farmland/grassland/heath/scrub/nature_reserve only (lawns never); planting stays null where frontage.inference is false. Woodland floor (#348): those classes also ship ground_texture.wood (podzol 0.30, coarse_dirt 0.10, moss_block 0.08, edge 2, scrub false) so natural=wood and landuse=forest replace the grass surface at lidar height, keeping grass within edge columns of the polygon; scrub stays on the pasture palette while scrub is false. New per-class keys join land_use.OPTIONAL_COLUMNS. Pure reader: lib/sources/land_use.py. Plan: docs/adr/006-land-use-classes.md. Woodland decor (#351): park, rural and natural ship woodland_decor shares for understorey bushes and ground cover inside natural=wood|scrub and landuse=forest (separate from planting, which stays null when frontage.inference is false); leaf_litter share ships 0 until #318 confirms 26.2 placement states. Typology (#428): palette, roofs and storeys on a class row are the plain default when a cell has no district profile, or the profile omits that class (ADR 006). Residential ships brick and a gable at exactly 2 storeys; commercial ships brick and a flat roof at exactly 2 storeys, so a missing building:levels has one count. A district profile replaces them, and the spec note names the class default when it is used. Other classes ship none until a trial names one. Terrace roofs (#441): residential ships terrace_roofs as roof-type names (red_clay_tile then grey_slate) so the typology terrace recipe can alternate pair colours; other classes omit it. Shopfront recipe (#431): commercial ships facade (front ground and upper glazing rows {glazed_h, pier}, one side row for the other faces, an entrance block with an awning kind and depth) and sign (default sign wood and text colour; the pair must clear the sign contrast floor). The typology generator emits the facade as facade_plan and the sign as signs, only for a building the street_face recipe does not already dress (a storey-1 facade_plan row on a street face switches the shopfront off in the builder; a dressed shop keeps its upper-storey and side windows, #466). Fascia colour is per building, never here. A class with neither key is generated as before.",
